.4 and 4.4.1 for MacOS\n\n### System information\n\nMacOS 15 Sequoia - Godot 4.4.1 - Macbook Pro M1\n\n### Issue description\n\nThe input fields for the X and Y values in the node in Visual Shader are displayed terribly tiny and overflow out of their area when filling the field value.\n\nThis only happens on macOS. I've also tried it on Windows 11 and Linux (Fedora 41), but there the error does not occur.\n\nIn the preview I am sending the UVFunc node for which I found the error, but it also happens for other nodes (e.g. DerivativeFunc for Vector2 sum)\n\nHere's an example of incorrect behaviour on macOS\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d010009a-6647-401a-91d7-19e3dfde25f1\n\nand an example of correct behaviour on Linux\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/de809911-97d6-47a8-996f-1333406487b6\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Create a new Visual Shader\n2. Add node with X and Y values (e.g. UVFunc or DerivativeFunc for Vector2 sum)\n3. Try to fill in the X and Y values\n\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions